{
  "meta": {
    "title": "mail storage toy: per-mailbox blob keys and real deletion on the real receive, IMAP and submission code",
    "status": "done",
    "date": "2026-11-03",
    "author": "platform",
    "track": "mail security"
  },
  "finding": "Per-mailbox keyed blob keys and erasure of objects work on the real code, but erasure from SQLite is not available to the application, so any text that must be erasable cannot be written to SQLite at all.",
  "premise": "Can blob keys stop being a shared plaintext hash, and can deleting mail really remove it, without breaking retries, redelivery, Sent, notices or open IMAP sessions?",
  "provenance": {
    "source_workflow": "One general-purpose agent, a patched copy of the real packages on local workerd, 8 predictions recorded first (01a1a48e-f9ae to 01a1a48e-fa05), all witnessed.",
    "method": "Real createReceiver, emailWorker and createImapSession, imaplib over a local TCP-to-WebSocket shim, R2 listings, byte scans of state files, kill -9 of the process tree. Two full runs; numbers from the last.",
    "verification": {
      "claims_held": 7,
      "refuted": 2,
      "unverifiable": 3
    },
    "tool_limits": "Local only. Not measured: D1 Time Travel (30 days paid, 7 free, per docs, no documented off switch), Durable Object recovery (30 days, per docs), production log storage, R2 after delete, production alarms, secret rotation, Mail.app or Thunderbird on an empty FETCH, a real 35-minute wait."
  },
  "claims": [
    {
      "claim": "2 objects, 2 after the repeat, 2 rows, hash parts differ",
      "status": "verified",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "toy-storage",
        "locator": "toy-storage/results.json"
      }
    },
    {
      "claim": "0 hits across 7 hashes in hex and base64, with the secret finding both keys as control",
      "status": "verified",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "toy-storage",
        "locator": "toy-storage/results.json"
      }
    },
    {
      "claim": "Gone 2.05 s after expunge with a 2 s window, UIDs 1 2 4, bytes off disk",
      "status": "verified",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "toy-storage",
        "locator": "toy-storage/results.json"
      }
    },
    {
      "claim": "OK with no data, connection open, also after hibernation. It holds as worded, but imaplib callers then raise TypeError, and RFC 2180 uses a tagged NO",
      "status": "verified",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "toy-storage",
        "locator": "toy-storage/results.json"
      }
    },
    {
      "claim": "Skipped with a keyed hash, EXISTS 0, id in no file. Unpredicted: the redelivery restores 1 object and 1 row with no sweep, and a message with no Message-ID returns as a new UID unless the blob key is kept",
      "status": "verified",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "toy-storage",
        "locator": "toy-storage/results.json"
      }
    },
    {
      "claim": "Hidden from a fresh SELECT, present with 3 s left, gone 0.06 s after the rule ended",
      "status": "verified",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "toy-storage",
        "locator": "toy-storage/results.json"
      }
    },
    {
      "claim": "10,000 rows gone and 0 objects left after 3 kills, but delete was issued twice for 500 keys, and resume took none within 60 s after 2 of 3 kills, 609.5 s total",
      "status": "verified",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "toy-storage",
        "locator": "toy-storage/results.json"
      }
    },
    {
      "claim": "A deleted row's text is absent from the local SQLite files without VACUUM.",
      "status": "refuted",
      "is_self_correction": true,
      "evidence": {
        "source": "toy-storage",
        "locator": "toy-storage/results.json#residue",
        "text": "Address text stayed in the D1 WAL after delete, clean stop, restart and 3,000 filler rows. The claim was false, at 0.40 confidence"
      }
    },
    {
      "claim": "After kill -9 an erase batch resumes in 0.13-0.26 s, as first reported.",
      "status": "refuted",
      "is_self_correction": true,
      "evidence": {
        "source": "toy-storage",
        "locator": "toy-storage/results.json#batch",
        "text": "alarm() sets its next alarm 300 s out before doing the work, so a kill after that write waits for it."
      }
    },
    {
      "claim": "Fix to the resume delay: a short retry alarm while an erase is pending.",
      "status": "unverified"
    },
    {
      "claim": "A tagged NO when every requested message is gone is what clients expect.",
      "status": "unverified"
    },
    {
      "claim": "A 35 m 10 s window: a 30-minute autologout that must be added, plus the 300 s alarm and 10 s tell bound. Only 2 s was tested, and a FETCH-only client is never bounded.",
      "status": "unverified"
    }
  ],
  "caveats": [
    "Deleted rows stay restorable for the platform's recovery window, so erasure can only promise a stated window per platform.",
    "PRAGMA secure_delete, wal_checkpoint and VACUUM are refused to the application in both D1 and Durable Objects.",
    "sending-worker.ts was changed in the copy to pass the secret, and that path did not run.",
    "Six type errors under workers-types are on lines unchanged from the original, which the repo type-checks without workers-types."
  ],
  "body": {
    "signatures": {
      "BlobKey": "(mailbox: string, bytes: Uint8Array) => Promise<string>",
      "Blobs": "{ put(key: string, bytes: Uint8Array): Promise<void>; erase(keys: string[]): Promise<void> } // a key already gone is no error; 1,000 per R2 call",
      "Deliveries": "{ record(row: DeliveryRow): Promise<void>; erase(ids: string[]): Promise<number> } // rows that went",
      "R2Like": "{ put(key: string, value: Uint8Array): Promise<unknown>; delete(keys: string | string[]): Promise<void> }",
      "mailbox object": "setRetention(until: number | null): Promise<void>",
      "ImapStore": "unchanged: bytes was already nullable and held returns tombstones"
    },
    "key_rule": "`${mailbox}/${HMAC-SHA256(secret, 'blob\\0' + mailbox + '\\0' + bytes)}`, with the label 'message-id' for the tombstone hash. createReceiver takes blobKey and does one put per mailbox, all before any record. SubmitInput loses blobKey, because core has no secret, and submitPorts derives it for `${mailbox}/Sent`. BLOB_SECRET goes on the receiving, IMAP, submission and sending workers. Mailbox ids must be opaque, since a lister can count per mailbox.",
    "erase_order": "D1 delete, R2 delete, then mark the row in one transaction. Reasoned from the code, not run: this order stops a racing redelivery leaving an object nothing names.",
    "must_hold": [
      "Stop writing deliveries.mail_from and rcpt_to: nothing in core, cloudflare, bridge or examples reads them. Hash the Message-ID from first sight.",
      "Sweep skipped deliveries too, or a redelivery or a retry brings erased bytes back. Three tries of a Sent copy or notice make 3 objects and 1 UID today.",
      "Keep the tombstone: removing the row closes a woken session with 1011, because restore needs every UID in its view. AUTOINCREMENT alone prevents UID reuse. The tombstone keeps the blob key as well as the hash, or a message with no Message-ID returns.",
      "Erasure arms its own alarm, since the chain only re-arms with a session registered.",
      "submissions and sends outlive the message with subject and recipients. Deleting sends makes a retry send again, so the send log needs its own decision.",
      "Sent has no deletion path, since LIST shows only INBOX.",
      "An untold session is still served retained bytes during a rule.",
      "holdKey is still an unkeyed SHA-256 of the mailbox and bytes. Rotating the secret breaks redelivery matching and key derivation."
    ],
    "null_fetch_today": "A session skips the message and answers tagged OK. A range returns what exists. FLAGS, RFC822.SIZE and INTERNALDATE answer from the tombstone, ENVELOPE gives nothing, SEARCH still lists it, STORE succeeds.",
    "code": "scratchpad/toy-storage (harness.py, results.json, storage.patch, src/index.ts, shim.ts, vendor/) in session d1068c98-86bb-4fa2-8415-63ac37e80e78"
  }
}
